<!-- language file start -->
title#:#Screen Magnifier
description#:#Screen magnifier with full-screen zoom up to 1600%, color inversion and a large mouse pointer – for all participants or only for listed users (special accommodations)
enable#:#Enable screen magnifier
enable_info#:#Provides visual aids in the test player: full-screen zoom with edge panning (nothing moves while the mouse stays in the center; near the screen edge the view glides in that direction – like the Windows Magnifier), color inversion and a large mouse pointer. Controlled via a floating bar in the bottom left corner and keyboard shortcuts (Ctrl+Alt+Plus/Minus, Ctrl+Alt+0 = reset zoom, Ctrl+Alt+I = inversion, Ctrl+Alt+P = pointer).
mode_label#:#Available for
mode_all#:#All participants
mode_all_info#:#Every participant sees the bar and can switch the aids on and off individually. Everything is off by default.
mode_list#:#Listed users only
mode_list_info#:#Only the users entered below see the bar (e.g. for special accommodations). All other participants will not notice the module at all.
user_list_label#:#User list
user_list_info#:#One entry per line (comma/semicolon also allowed): ILIAS login name or matriculation number. Case-insensitive.
allow_zoom#:#Allow full-screen zoom
allow_zoom_info#:#Magnifies the entire page. The center of the screen is a calm zone for reading and clicking; only near the screen edge does the view pan in that direction. All inputs keep working normally.
max_zoom_label#:#Maximum magnification
allow_invert#:#Allow color inversion
allow_invert_info#:#Inverts the page colors (light text on dark background). Images and videos keep their original colors.
allow_cursor#:#Allow large mouse pointer
allow_cursor_info#:#Replaces the mouse pointer with a large yellow pointer and highlights clicks with a short ring animation.
js_tb_label#:#Visual aids
js_tb_open#:#Show visual aids
js_tb_close#:#Hide visual aids
js_zoom_in#:#Zoom in (Ctrl+Alt+Plus)
js_zoom_out#:#Zoom out (Ctrl+Alt+Minus)
js_invert#:#Invert colors (Ctrl+Alt+I)
js_cursor#:#Large mouse pointer (Ctrl+Alt+P)
js_deadzone#:#Calm zone – move the mouse to the screen edge to pan
